### Auth Middleware Test

### 1. Register a user first
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "first_name": "John",
  "last_name": "Doe",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "phone_number": "+1234567890",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 2. Login to get access token
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 3. Test protected endpoint with valid token (replace YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN

### 4. Test protected endpoint without token (should fail)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/me

### 5. Test protected endpoint with invalid token (should fail)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer invalid_token_here

### 6. Test order creation with valid token (should work and use user_id from context)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "restaurantId": "restaurant-123",
  "restaurantName": "Pizza Palace",
  "items": [
    {
      "foodId": "food-123",
      "name": "Margherita Pizza",
      "price": 15.99,
      "quantity": 2,
      "specialInstructions": "Extra cheese"
    }
  ],
  "subtotal": 31.98,
  "deliveryFee": 3.99,
  "tax": 2.88,
  "total": 38.85,
  "deliveryAddress": "123 Main St, New York, NY 10001",
  "paymentMethodId": "card-123",
  "notes": "Ring doorbell twice"
}

### 7. Test order creation without token (should fail)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "restaurantId": "restaurant-123",
  "restaurantName": "Pizza Palace",
  "items": [
    {
      "foodId": "food-123",
      "name": "Margherita Pizza",
      "price": 15.99,
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "subtotal": 15.99,
  "deliveryFee": 3.99,
  "tax": 1.44,
  "total": 21.42,
  "deliveryAddress": "123 Main St, New York, NY 10001",
  "paymentMethodId": "card-123"
}

### 8. Test user profile endpoint with valid token
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/users/USER_ID_HERE
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN

### 9. Test user profile endpoint without token (should fail)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/users/USER_ID_HERE